From 33bc2a1131cc875777f7b5d24aaff163115af154 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Vasconcelos <Felipe.Vasconcelos@windriver.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 15:39:30 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Ship openstack_auth message catalogs in the package

The Debian MANIFEST.in (as amended by fixed-horizon-MANIFEST.in.patch)
grafts data files for doc, horizon and openstack_dashboard, but has no
entry for openstack_auth. Its compiled gettext catalogs (*.mo) are
therefore dropped from python3-django-horizon, so every
openstack_auth-only string - the login "Authenticate using" selector
label, auth-method and password-change prompts, and the authentication
status messages - falls back to English even though upstream ships a
translated zh_Hans catalog for them. Strings that also exist in
horizon/openstack_dashboard (Password, Domain, User Name) render
translated because those catalogs are shipped.

Add a recursive-include for openstack_auth mirroring the other grafts so
its compiled catalogs are packaged. This ships the already-present
upstream translations for all languages; no translation content is
authored here.

Signed-off-by: Felipe Vasconcelos <Felipe.Vasconcelos@windriver.com>
---
 MANIFEST.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/MANIFEST.in b/MANIFEST.in
index ef9a297..330b4b0 100644
--- a/MANIFEST.in
+++ b/MANIFEST.in
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 recursive-include doc *
 recursive-include horizon *
 recursive-include openstack_dashboard *
+recursive-include openstack_auth *
 recursive-include tools *.py *.sh
 recursive-include openstack_dashboard/conf *
 
